{
  "scores": {
    "pmf": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "Forks provide a provisional developer-interest signal [c3], but active downstream use and independent contributors are unverified. Displaying ecosystem transaction volumes [c2] does not establish transactions through Merit, customer retention or willingness to pay; aggregate stars [c4] do not resolve those gaps."
    },
    "narrative": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "The explorer, API framework and agent template form a coherent agent-commerce story [c1, c2, c6, c7]. However, the sources do not establish a differentiated commercial edge, validated demand for the broader suite or a credible path from discovery to a defensible platform."
    },
    "execution": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "Commit activity and the recent explorer push support active development [c8, c9, c10]. Contributor breadth, release quality and responsiveness to standards changes remain unknown; an invitation to contribute [c11] does not establish contributions from multiple people."
    }
  },
  "recommendation": "watch",
  "unsupported_claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "reason": "The quote supports the stated vision but omits the stablecoin and just-in-time purchasing assertion. That assertion appears elsewhere in the supplied document, but requires a receipt covering that passage."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c8",
      "reason": "The metric supports the commit count, and FACTS supplies its scope, but the claim includes additional numbers for repository count, window length and cutoff date that do not equal the cited metric value. The receipt fails the stated numeric rule."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c9",
      "reason": "The cited metric supports the prior-window count only. The recent count requires its own metric receipt; referencing it in this claim violates the stated numeric rule."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c11",
      "reason": "The quote establishes recruitment of contributors only. It does not substantiate the monorepo components or the specific resource and facilitator contribution workflows, although those appear elsewhere in the document."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c14",
      "reason": "The receipt supports rank only. The candidate-pool size requires a separate receipt using screen.n_candidates; screening rank also does not independently validate market demand."
    }
  ],
  "missing_risks": [
    "External maintainer participation and ownership concentration are unknown, leaving key-person risk unresolved.",
    "The memo should distinguish economically meaningful, recurring agent purchases from experimental, subsidized or automated ecosystem activity; displayed transaction volume alone cannot settle this.",
    "Explorer coverage and attribution may depend on which facilitators and resources are registered, creating potential completeness and measurement risks [d_dcd4dbd8e9e6ee95].",
    "Embedded-wallet access raises security and transaction-authorization diligence questions; the sources do not establish custody arrangements, audits or controls [c2].",
    "Developer interest may attach primarily to ecosystem discovery rather than the commercial API tooling, so conversion between products remains unproven [c3, c6, c7]."
  ],
  "strongest_counterargument": "The strongest case against advancing is that repository activity and ecosystem visibility have not yet demonstrated a specific customer repeatedly using or paying for Merit's products. Without verified adoption quality and a credible value-capture mechanism, the evidence supports continued monitoring more strongly than investment progression."
}
